        "title": "Resource Imbalance Alert",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>During a zombie apocalypse, survivor bases manage scarce resources. Anomalies occur when supply quantities and survivor counts exhibit specific mathematical relationships, indicating vulnerability to undead hordes. Security teams prioritize aid to these unstable bases. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'bases', 'survivors': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'bases' table includes columns 'base_id', 'base_name', and 'location', representing the base's unique ID, its designated name, and its geographical area. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'survivors' table includes columns 'survivor_id', 'base_id', and 'supply_count', representing the survivor's unique ID, their assigned base ID, and the units of resources they possess. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that: &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Processes only bases located in 'Downtown', 'Suburbs', or 'Rural' zones &nbsp;</li>\n<li>For each such base, sum all survivors&rsquo; <em data-start=\"495\" data-end=\"509\">supply_count</em> to get <em data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"533\">total_supplies</em>, and count its survivors to get <em data-start=\"566\" data-end=\"582\">survivor_count</em>.</li>\n<li>Identifies bases where total supplies and survivor counts meet one of two instability conditions: &nbsp;<br />\n<ul>\n<li>Total supplies are even while survivor count is odd &nbsp;</li>\n<li>Total supplies are divisible by 3 while survivor count is divisible by 5 &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'base_name', 'total_supplies', and 'survivor_count', ordered by base_name in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE bases (\n    base_id INT,\n    base_name VARCHAR(20),\n    location VARCHAR(10)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE survivors (\n    survivor_id INT,\n    base_id INT,\n    supply_count INT\n);\nINSERT INTO bases (base_id, base_name, location) VALUES\n(1, 'Base Alpha', 'Downtown'),\n(2, 'Base Bravo', 'Suburbs'),\n(3, 'Base Charlie', 'Rural'),\n(4, 'Base Delta', 'Downtown');\nINSERT INTO survivors (survivor_id, base_id, supply_count) VALUES\n(1, 1, 4),\n(2, 1, 5),\n(3, 1, 3),\n(4, 2, 6),\n(5, 2, 1),\n(6, 3, 10),\n(7, 3, 7),\n(8, 4, 2),\n(9, 4, 1);",
        "slug": "resource-imbalance-alert",
