        "description": "<p>The pet store analyzes sales data for high-value animals. Management requires a revenue report for premium pet categories during a promotional month to evaluate marketing effectiveness. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given one table: 'pet_sales': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'pet_sales' table includes the columns 'sale_id', 'pet_type', 'sale_date', and 'price', representing unique sale identifiers, pet categories, sale dates, and sale prices in dollars. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that: &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Calculates total revenue and average price for dogs, cats, and birds sold during November 2023. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>Returns only categories where the average price exceeds $100. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'pet_type', 'total_revenue', and 'avg_price', ordered by total_revenue descending.</p>",
