        "title": "Remainder Report",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>In the Cyber Caf&eacute; and adjacent Fire Department, administrators want to see how activity distributes across machine and station IDs by their remainder when divided by three. This will help them balance maintenance schedules across the network.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;cafe_sessions&rsquo; and &lsquo;firecalls&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"157\" data-end=\"258\">The 'cafe_sessions' table includes the columns 'session_id', 'machine_id', and 'user_name'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"352\">The 'firecalls' table includes the columns 'call_id', 'station_id', and 'incident'.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"354\" data-end=\"370\">Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"374\" data-end=\"514\">For each cafe session, compute the remainder of machine_id divided by 3, then count how many sessions fall into each remainder category.</li>\n<li data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"651\">For each fire call, compute the remainder of station_id divided by 3, then count how many calls fall into each remainder category.</li>\n<li data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"847\">Combine these counts by remainder so that each remainder value (0, 1, 2) shows the total session_count and the corresponding call_count (defaulting to 0 if no calls match that remainder).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'remainder', 'session_count', and 'call_count', ordered by remainder ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE cafe_sessions (\n  session_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  machine_id INT,\n  user_name VARCHAR(100)\n);\nCREATE TABLE firecalls (\n  call_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  station_id INT,\n  incident VARCHAR(100)\n);\nINSERT INTO cafe_sessions VALUES\n  (101, 110, 'Grace'),\n  (102, 111, 'Hank'),\n  (103, 112, 'Ivy'),\n  (104, 113, 'Jake'),\n  (105, 114, 'Kara');\nINSERT INTO firecalls VALUES\n  (101, 210, 'Alarm X'),\n  (102, 211, 'Alarm Y'),\n  (103, 212, 'Alarm Z'),\n  (104, 213, 'Alarm W'),\n  (105, 214, 'Alarm V');\n\n",
        "slug": "remainder-report",
