        "description": "<p>The lunar base coordinates gym workouts with base activities to monitor astronaut health and resource usage. Management requires identifying distinct astronauts who had highly efficient days (burning significant calories while conserving oxygen) during November 2023. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'gym_workouts' and 'lunar_activities': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'gym_workouts' table includes the columns 'workout_id', 'astronaut_id', 'workout_date', 'calories_burned', and 'duration_minutes', representing unique workout identifiers, astronaut identifiers, workout dates, calories burned, and workout duration. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'lunar_activities' table includes the columns 'activity_id', 'astronaut_id', 'activity_date', 'oxygen_consumed_liters', and 'activity_type', representing unique activity identifiers, astronaut identifiers, activity dates, oxygen consumed in liters, and activity categories. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Joins workouts and activities for the same 'astronaut_id' on matching dates within November 2023.</li>\n<li>Aggregates per astronaut per date the total 'calories_burned' and total 'oxygen_consumed_liters'.</li>\n<li>Identifies distinct astronauts who had at least one day meeting: &nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &bull; Total calories burned &gt; 500 &nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &bull; Total oxygen consumed &gt; 50 &nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &bull; Efficiency ratio (calories &divide; oxygen) &gt; 10 &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include only the column 'astronaut_id', ordered by astronaut_id ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE gym_workouts (\n    workout_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    astronaut_id INT,\n    workout_date DATE,\n    calories_burned INT,\n    duration_minutes INT\n);\nINSERT INTO gym_workouts VALUES\n(1, 101, '2023-11-10', 400, 60),\n(2, 101, '2023-11-10', 300, 45),\n(3, 102, '2023-11-15', 700, 60),\n(4, 103, '2023-11-20', 600, 50),\n(5, 104, '2023-12-05', 800, 70);\n\nCREATE TABLE lunar_activities (\n    activity_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    astronaut_id INT,\n    activity_date DATE,\n    oxygen_consumed_liters INT,\n    activity_type VARCHAR(50)\n);\nINSERT INTO lunar_activities VALUES\n(101, 101, '2023-11-10', 40, 'EVA'),\n(102, 101, '2023-11-10', 15, 'Maintenance'),\n(103, 102, '2023-11-15', 60, 'EVA'),\n(104, 103, '2023-11-20', 30, 'Maintenance'),\n(105, 104, '2023-12-05', 70, 'Research');\n\n",
