        "description": "<p>The alien zoo monitors habitat conditions for extraterrestrial species. Zookeepers require an enclosure-level report categorizing temperature compliance to prioritize climate adjustments. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'species' and 'enclosures': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'species' table includes the columns 'species_id', 'species_name', 'enclosure_id', and 'optimal_temperature', representing unique species identifiers, species names, enclosure IDs, and ideal temperatures in Celsius. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'enclosures' table includes the columns 'enclosure_id', 'enclosure_name', and 'current_temperature', representing unique enclosure identifiers, enclosure names, and current temperatures in Celsius. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that: &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>For each enclosure, counts species in three temperature categories: &nbsp;\n<ul>\n<li>'Too Cold': current_temperature &le; optimal_temperature - 5 &nbsp;</li>\n<li>'Too Hot': current_temperature &ge; optimal_temperature + 5 &nbsp;</li>\n<li>'Optimal': within &plusmn;4&deg;C of optimal &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Returns enclosures with at least one species in non-optimal conditions. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'enclosure_name', 'too_cold_count', 'too_hot_count', and 'optimal_count', ordered by too_cold_count descending and enclosure_name ascending.</p>",
